 { Now, as Krasenkow points out, White should have played: } 37. Qa1 { In fact, I like this move so much I will leave it as the main variation. } ( { Instead, Malakhov spoiled his position with } 37. gxh6 $2 { throwing away his positional edge and weakening his structure. } Nh5 { Now Black threatens to play ...Nxd5 , so: } 38. Qa7 Kh7 39. Bh4 $2 { This careless move allows Black to take the lead } ( { better was } 39. Qa1 Bf6 40. Qd1 Kxh6 41. Kg2 $11 { which should be drawn } ) 
