14. a3 Bd7 15. b4 b6 16. Rae1 ( { The alternative } 16. bxc5 bxc5 17. Rab1 Re8 18. Kh2 Rb8 { gives White only the tiny advantage that is typical of this structure. } ) 
Re8 17. Ng3 Rxe1 18. Rxe1 Qf8 { This simple move is very effective, as after ...Re8 White’s advantage will only be symbolic. } 19. Be2 $6 { White starts to go down the wrong path; retaining control of the e4-square is essential. } ( { A plausible line was } 19. Qb3 Re8 20. Rxe8 Ncxe8 21. Be3 { with equality. } ) 
Re8 20. Rb1 $6 { Going even further away from e4. } Ne4 $1 { Black has gained the initiative by understanding the importance of controlling e4. } 21. Ncxe4 fxe4 22. Rf1 ( { The pawn cannot be taken by } 22. Nxe4 $2 { because of } Rxe4 $1 23. Qxe4 Bf5 { when the rook on b1 is hanging. } ) 
Bd4+ 23. Kh2 Qe7 ( { An interesting alternative was } 23... e3 24. Be1 Qg7 { with an unclear position. } ) 
